Perhaps I was unclear. I'm not saying that the iPhone doesn't have some 
very good games: tt probably has a wider choice of good games, but so far 
as I know there's nothing about the iPhone that makes it a better gaming 
platform. Both systems have the same screen resolution, similar graphics 
capabilities, accelerometer, capacitive touch screen.

Android has a lower barrier to entry (you don't have to pay for the SDK) 
but also a smaller target market (so far). Since I doubt anyone is going to 
get rich selling Nethack on either device the potential market probably 
isn't very significant.

Some Android devices of course have a keyboard, so to that extent they're 
more promising for Nethack than the iPhone, but most of the recent Androids 
don't have a keyboard either.

